ToGet a Range of a Array
var names = new List<string> { "David", "Sage", "Maria" };
names.Add("Michael");
names.Remove("Sage");

foreach (var name in names[2..4])
{
    Console.WriteLine($"Hello {name}!");
}

// This gets you the 2nd 3rd value in the array.
// The .. operator is used to specify a range of indices in the array. In this case, it gets the elements at index 2 and 3 (the 3rd and 4th elements) from the names list. The output will be:



